# Files that are copied into Linux images must keep LF endings regardless of
# the platform they are checked out on. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look
# for an interpreter named "/bin/sh\r", so the script fails to exec and the
# container healthcheck never passes.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
.env text eol=lf
